    "analysis_type": "paradigm_network",
    "rationale": "Only one defensible construction survives strict joint testing: a targeted-action family in which several action stems alternate before the same suffix @X, and each whole meaning is compositionally predictable from the stem meaning plus a stable 'specified face or location' contribution. I reject the other hinted families: STONE@X vs STONE~X does show a contrast, but assigning STONE@X simultaneously to that family and to the broader @X family is impossible under the required partition, and the broader @X paradigm is better supported by multiple alternating stems in one frame. The BELL/BELL-ALT, REST/REST@X, stable/stall, ALL/BELL, CORNERS/COLD, and HOT/HOLLOW hints fail the compositional-paradigm test: their residues do not form a stable substitution class with predictable shared roles. Standalone location terms (B, T, N, S, E, W, ALL, OPP, EDGES, CORNERS) remain lexical symbols because no concrete multi-morpheme code instantiates them here, but they support the interpretation of X as the target variable in the surviving family.",
